  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "calycosin_selected_virtual_modes_have_positive_observed_curvature",
      "statement": "For original calycosin virtual-mode directions 1 and 7, both step sizes give positive central energy and gradient curvatures, opposing the saved negative analytic Hessian predictions. These selected observations do not support a real saddle interpretation along those directions."
    },
    {
      "id": "calycosin_positive_control_also_has_magnitude_error",
      "statement": "Original positive mode8 remains positive but energy curvature is about 0.006928 rather than analytic 0.0012325 Eh/Bohr^2, showing a large magnitude mismatch beyond virtual-mode signs."
    },
    {
      "id": "acid_positive_mode1_curvature_robust_to_grid_and_response_controls",
      "statement": "Acid mode1 observed curvature remains positive with denser grid3/noresponse and with grid1/full gradient grid response. These controls do not recover the large saved negative analytic prediction."
    },
    {
      "id": "gradient_grid_response_reduces_small_energy_gradient_gap",
      "statement": "At acid mode1 grid1, enabling gradient grid response reduces |energy-curvature minus gradient-curvature| from approximately 2.4e-5 to 6.3e-7/7.1e-7 Eh/Bohr^2, about a 34–38 fold reduction. This explains a smaller energy/gradient consistency effect, not the approximately 0.057 Eh/Bohr^2 analytic-versus-observed sign discrepancy."
    }
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "All original Hessian matrices remain unchanged. Grid3 tests here are fresh energy/gradient differences at the original geometry, not newly computed analytic grid3 Hessians.",
    "Original analytic Hessians used SCF energy tolerance 1e-8; displaced observations use 1e-10, and no independent CPHF residual has been measured.",
    "Only selected mode directions are covered. Positive selected curvatures do not establish all-mode positivity or stable minima, nor prove that every saved imaginary mode is spurious.",
    "Finite quadrature response, derivative backend behavior and other numerical causes remain distinct hypotheses. These observations do not isolate a unique implementation defect.",
    "The calycosin grid3 comparison was still pending when this review was created."
  ],
  "IR_intensities_status": "NOT_COMPUTED"
}
